From 0595b46c751e16deff8473d0ce1bf04f11eedc19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Francesco Pham <francesco.pham1@h-partners.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 13:49:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] surface: don't report missing metadata support as an error

SurfaceBufferImpl::SetMetadata treated DISPLAY_NOT_SUPPORT as a failure:
a BLOGE per call, and GSERROR_HDI_ERROR handed back to the caller. But a
display buffer VDI with no metadata channel answers NOT_SUPPORT to every
call - the reference implementation in display/buffer/vdi_base does
exactly that - and RSUniRenderComposerAdapter::SetBufferColorSpace sets
metadata on every composed buffer. So this logged from the render thread
on every frame, for the life of the device. Measured on the Plinius at
57 lines/s; together with the two logs it triggers either side of it,
86% of everything reaching hilog.

Return GSERROR_NOT_SUPPORT without logging, which is how RegisterBuffer
in this same file already handles the identical answer. Genuine HDI
failures are untouched: still logged, still GSERROR_HDI_ERROR.

Change-Id: I26b8f7bc6020e88e90addb0b0150baed4172bb2a
Signed-off-by: Francesco Pham <francesco.pham1@h-partners.com>
---
 surface/src/surface_buffer_impl.cpp | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/surface/src/surface_buffer_impl.cpp b/surface/src/surface_buffer_impl.cpp
index 08c97d7..9b8ea5f 100644
--- a/surface/src/surface_buffer_impl.cpp
+++ b/surface/src/surface_buffer_impl.cpp
@@ -798,6 +798,16 @@ GSError SurfaceBufferImpl::SetMetadata(uint32_t key, const std::vector<uint8_t>&
         }
         return GSERROR_OK;
     }
+    // A VDI with no metadata channel answers NOT_SUPPORT to every call - the
+    // reference implementation in display/buffer/vdi_base does exactly that.
+    // That is an answer, not a failure, and callers set metadata on every
+    // composed buffer, so reporting it as an error logs from the render thread
+    // on every frame. RegisterBuffer above already declines to treat the same
+    // answer as an error; report it distinctly here rather than as OK, so a
+    // caller that cares can tell "no metadata support" from "stored nothing".
+    if (dRet == GRAPHIC_DISPLAY_NOT_SUPPORT) {
+        return GSERROR_NOT_SUPPORT;
+    }
     BLOGE("SetMetadata Failed with %{public}d", dRet);
     return GSERROR_HDI_ERROR;
 }
-- 
